    "lawCode": "Amd §§3602 & 579, Pub Health L; amd §§902 & 903, Ed L; amd §§406, 433 & 434, Gen Bus L; amd §§404-a & 509-g, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S2300\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, the education law, the general\nbusiness law and the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to making\nconforming changes reflecting the previously authorized scope of\npractice of nurse practitioners\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo conform various sections of law with the 2014 legislation in\nrelation to nurse practitioner (NP) written collaboration or practice\nagreements. It would not affect any scope of practice.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSections 1 through 5 and 8 through 10 remove many references to NPs\nperforming various functions in accordance with a written practice\nagreement and replaces them with references to the NP acting in his or\nher lawful scope of practice, which would mean in accordance with a\nwritten practice agreement where that is applicable and in accordance\nwith a collaborative relationship where that is applicable.\n\nSection 1 amends PHL § 3602(4) and (5), relating to an NP prescribing\nor ordering home care services.\n\nSection 2 amends PHL § 579 (1), relating to NPs providing clinical\nlaboratory test solely as an adjunct to the treatment of a patient.\n\nSection 3 amends Education Law § 902 (2)(a), relating to NPs\nperforming school health services.\n\nSection 4 amends Education Law § 903(1), relating to NPs providing\nprimary and secondary school health certificates.\n\nSection 5 amends General Business Law § 406 (1)(e), relating to NPs\nproviding cosmetology health certificates.\n\nSections 6 and 7 amend General Business Law §§ 433(3) and 434 to\npermit NPs to provide and certify physical exams for barber license\napplicants.\n\nSections 8 and 9 amend Vehicle and Traffic Law § 404-a(4) and (5)(b),\nrelation to NPs providing certificates of disability.\n\nSection 10 amends Vehicle and Traffic Law § 509-g(1), relating to NPs\nproviding bus driver health certificates.\n\nSection 11 clarifies that the preceding sections shall not be\nconstrued to expand or contract the NP scope of practice.\n\nSection 12 provides an effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\n\nThe Nurse Practice Act in the Education Law was amended in 2014 to\neliminate the requirement of a written practice agreement for NPs with\nover 3600 hours of practice experience. The amendments in this bill\nare necessary to eliminate now-inappropriate references to agreements\nthat are no longer required. The Nurse Practice Act provides the\nnecessary requirements for NPs whose practice experience is less than\n3600 hours (who work under a written collaboration or practice\nagreement) and others (who work under a collaborative relationship).\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nThis bill would have no fiscal impact on the State or local\ngovernments.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nImmediately.\n\n",
